        },
        "content": "<div style='background:#eff6ff;border:1px solid #bfdbfe;border-radius:8px;padding:16px 24px'><h3 style='margin:0 0 8px'>🔧 Modular System Architecture</h3><p style='margin:0 0 12px;color:#374151'>FarmSense Brew's modular design allows independent monitoring of multiple 50 sqm zones. Each zone operates autonomously with its own:</p><ul style='color:#374151;margin:0;padding-left:20px;line-height:1.8'><li><strong>ESP32 Sensor Network:</strong> 5 nodes (DHT22 + Capacitive Soil Moisture v1.2) in X formation</li><li><strong>Irrigation Control:</strong> Independent solenoid valve per node with CLR-aware logic</li><li><strong>Data Pipeline:</strong> Node-RED processing → MySQL storage → Dashboard visualization</li><li><strong>Dashboard Integration:</strong> All zones visible across Agronomist, Farm Owner, and Field Staff views</li></ul><p style='margin:12px 0 0;color:#6b7280;font-style:italic'>Each additional zone can be registered, configured, and monitored independently, demonstrating the system's capacity for incremental farm expansion beyond the pilot plot.</p></div>",
        "mode": "html"
